3.  the phantom maximum, for the kernel the data follow
====================================================================================================================
  For nu_RAR the phantom acceleration is g_ph = g_bar (nu - 1) = a_0 y e^{-sqrt y}/(1 - e^{-sqrt y}).  Its maximum:
     max g_ph = 0.6476 a_0  at  g_bar = 2.540 a_0   (mu_exp instead: 1/e = 0.368 a_0 at 0.632 a_0)
     in m/s^2: 6.062e-11 (canonical), 7.318e-11 (alt)
  [PASS] P1 (THE NUMBER) the observed phantom acceleration near its predicted peak matches the nu_RAR maximum within the galaxy-level error: no SPARC galaxy's dark acceleration exceeds ~0.66 a_0   (observed max in the window 8.83 +/- 3.79 x 1e-11 m/s^2; predicted 6.06 at g_bar = 2.54 a_0)
  [PASS] P2 the observed phantom TURNS OVER: the well-populated bins above the peak sit below it, as any kernel with a Newtonian limit requires and as the 'simple' kernel (phantom -> a_0, never declining) forbids   (bins at log y in (0.75, 1.45]: max 6.63 vs peak 8.83 (x1e-11); N bins 3)

====================================================================================================================
4.  mutation controls
====================================================================================================================
  [PASS] M1 mutation: shuffling g_obs across points destroys the relation for both kernels, so S1/S2 are structure in the data and not in the binning   (shuffled residual power far exceeds the real one)
  [PASS] M2 mutation: the two kernels are numerically identical in both limits (deep MOND: g = sqrt(g_bar a_0); Newtonian: g = g_bar), so the rejection in S2 is a TRANSITION-shape statement and cannot be blamed on either limit   (both limits agree to <0.005 dex)

====================================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  The repository has been running two kernels and calling them one.  The empirical nu_RAR = 1/(1-e^{-sqrt y}) and
  the field-theory 'exact exponential' mu_exp = 1-e^{-x} share both limits and differ by up to ~0.08 dex in the
  transition, and SPARC decides between them: chi^2(mu_exp) - chi^2(nu_RAR) = 163 on 18 galaxy-level bins, with
  transition pulls of up to 7 sigma against mu_exp.  The data follow nu_RAR (which was fitted to them) and reject
  mu_exp.  Every completion gate that demanded 'exact mu_exp' -- CDE-L4C, HPI-Delta, the regular-center coefficients,
  the alpha_1 drag term -- was built to reproduce a transition the data do not have.  The obstruction results are
  about the SHAPE class (a deep-MOND limit, an exponential Newtonian tail), which both kernels share, so they are
  not undone; but gate 1 as written ('mu = 1 - e^{-y} exactly') is the wrong target, and the right one is nu_RAR's
  mu, which has no closed form.  The phantom-acceleration maximum for the kernel the data follow is
  0.648 a_0 at g_bar = 2.54 a_0 (6.06e-11 m/s^2 canonical), observed 8.83 +/- 3.79 x 1e-11: a universal
  ceiling on the dark acceleration in galaxies, set by the cosmological constant.

